<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">attentĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		attendo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>attentiveness</i>, <i>attention</i>,
				<i>application.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> With <i>animi</i>: reliqua sunt in curā, attentione animi, cogitatione, vigilantiā, etc., <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 2, 35, 150</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">docilem sine dubio et haec ipsa praestat
					attentio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 4, 1, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum (servos) tantā
					cruciāsti attentione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Sap. 12, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
